  "body": "Patch SignalR Redis and its required Options/DependencyInjection.Abstractions closure to 10.0.15 on the retained 4.44 maintenance line. The source keeps the normal signed G4 package/archive/inventory lifecycle and adds exact-source, latest-attempt and complete-job release checks from the approved maintenance policy.\n\nThe workflow changes are generated by owner policy 3c285357c9eadec74a3516d649c8197fe1719052, delivered in https://github.com/Hexalith/Hexalith.CiCd/pull/1. Main stays on its existing source line. The proof will execute the separately frozen released 4.48.2 tool.\n\nValidation: 15 transport/boundary controls passed; actual SDK 10.0.403 restore controls prove the minimal three-pin dependency closure; locked dependency signatures and both full commit messages passed. The installed normal analyzer derives patch 4.44.14 from actual v4.44.13 ancestry. Normal PR CI and exact-source push CI must pass before protected publication; no tag has been created.\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Touches protected release/CI publication gates and semantic-release branch config, though the maintenance path adds fail-closed checks and extensive contract tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Patches the **4.44** central package catalog by bumping **SignalR.StackExchangeRedis**, **DependencyInjection.Abstractions**, and **Options** to **10.0.15**, keeping the minimal closure aligned with the maintenance line.\n> \n> Adds a bounded **`4.44.x`** release lane end-to-end: **semantic-release** gains a `4.44.x` branch/range, **CI** runs on that branch, and **`4.44.x` dispatches** use a new **`verify-maintenance-release-source.py`** gate (approved ancestry, frozen live tip, latest successful push CI attempt, and required jobs) instead of the main/prerelease path. **Release** workflows retain maintenance verification receipts as artifacts, qualification tooling accepts **`refs/heads/4.44.x`**, and new **Python contract tests** plus updated **G4/release contract** checks lock the behavior in.\n> \n> A small **workspace MSBuild** test expectation update reflects which late **HXW** property is asserted when **Configuration** conflicts with source vs dependency mode.\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 3aafeda8ed2b2befa0f49c78fe0b5c88c79d7f1c. Bugbot is set up for automated code reviews on this repo. Configure [here](https://www.cursor.com/dashboard/bugbot).</sup>\n<!-- /CURSOR_SUMMARY -->",
